WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:06.120
Did you ever wonder if certain foods
have a direct effect on your health?

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.120
Well, I’m here to
solve that mystery

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.560
since you are
the foods you eat.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.640
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.440
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:22.000
In this series, we look at the history,
benefits, and safety of water fluoridation.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.200
And we start by looking at the efficacy
of adding fluoride to the water supply.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.960
A meta-analysis
of all the studies

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.440
on the dental health
implications

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.120
of vegetarian diets

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.600
showed significantly
fewer decayed teeth,

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.560
missing teeth,

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.160
and the number of teeth
with fillings.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.960
One of the studies
that bucked the trend

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.080
and showed that
vegetarians had more cavities

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.360
blamed the excess decay
on the fact that vegetarians

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.800
were significantly
less likely to choose

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.040
fluoride-containing toothpaste,

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.840
supported by the fact
that those who did use

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.800
toothpaste with fluoride
had significantly fewer

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.200
decayed teeth
than those who didn't.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.240
Fluoride is thought to protect
teeth by improving the intrinsic

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.360
stability of the mineral
structure of dental enamel.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.520
A recent meta-analysis of nearly
100 randomized controlled trials

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.480
of fluoride toothpaste involving
more than 10,000 people

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.120
found "high-certainty" evidence

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.120
that toothpaste containing
the typical amount of fluoride

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.280
reduces tooth decay
significantly more

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.520
than non-fluoride toothpaste
in both children and adults.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.400
But what about the addition
of fluoride to the water supply?

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.560
A medical consensus

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.320
of public health authorities
around the world

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.880
has considered
water fluoridation

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:27.720
at appropriate levels

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.280
as a safe and effective means

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.200
to prevent cavities
on a community-wide scale.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.880
In fact, the CDC,

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.200
the US Centers for Disease
Control and Prevention,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.360
deemed fluoridation
of drinking water

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.720
as one of the top ten
public health achievements

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.960
of the 20th century.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.440
However, community
water fluoridation

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:48.120
has long been a flashpoint
of polemic and polarization.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.320
Anti-fluoridation activists
underscore that there is

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.400
no human dietary
requirement for fluoride

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.360
and argue that
water fluoridation

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.240
isn't effective enough
to justify the costs,

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:59.840
which may include health risks.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.680
First, some background before
I dive into the controversy.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.000
Fluoride is a mineral element
in the Earth's crust

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.600
that naturally occurs
in most water supplies.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.120
This is one of the reasons
fluoridation has withstood

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.760
Constitutional challenges.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.960
Courts have ruled that,
rather than an added medication,

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.280
fluoride can be seen as
a nutrient found naturally

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.920
in some areas but not others,

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.360
and fluoridation
of water supplies

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.960
is a matter of just
leveling the playing field,

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.360
particularly for
poor communities

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.880
who may have limited access
to dental care.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.080
Fluoridation can be defined as

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.640
"the upward
or downward adjustment

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.720
of the level of fluoride
content in drinking water

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.640
to an optimal level
just enough to prevent cavities

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.800
but not enough
to cause fluorosis,"

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.360
or cosmetic changes
to the teeth.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.960
It all started in 1901

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.480
with an investigation
into Colorado Brown Stain,

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.160
"grotesque" brown stains

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.400
on the teeth
of Colorado Springs residents.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.160
At the same time, teeth
afflicted by the condition were

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.520
"surprisingly and inexplicably
resistant to decay."

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.680
After fluoride was identified
as the basis for these changes,

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.600
a nationwide survey of fluoride
levels in drinking water

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.480
in the 1930s
led to the discovery

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.160
that fluoride could reach levels
around 1 part per million

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.960
without causing
serious fluorosis.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.880
Hoping to get
the best of both worlds,

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.920
Grand Rapids, Michigan, in 1945,

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.520
became the first city
in the world

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.680
to fluoridate its water supply.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.520
Within 11 years, cavity rates
among children in Grand Rapids

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.480
were reportedly down
more than 60 percent,

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.840
and a fluoridation
movement was born.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.240
Today, about two dozen countries
fluoridate their drinking water.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.040
Dozens of others have
naturally fluoridated water

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.240
or instead add fluoride
to milk or table salt.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:47.800
Fluoridation pushback
started almost immediately

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.080
in the United States.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.240
The obsession
of Dr. Strangelove's

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:55.480
Colonel Ripper with the purity
of his "precious bodily fluids"

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.000
was based on real-life
right-wing Red Scare

00:03:59.000 --> 00:03:59.960
conspiracy theories

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.640
that fluoridation
was meant to produce

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.880
"moronic, atheistic slaves"
who would bow to the communists.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.480
Today's social media
is also rife

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.960
with anti-fluoridation messages.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.520
Studies have found that 63
percent of Instagram posts

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.080
regarding fluoride could be
classified as anti-fluoride,

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.840
64 percent of tweets on Twitter,

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:19.960
99 percent of YouTube videos,

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.560
and up to 100 percent
of fluoride groups and pages

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.520
found on Facebook
were anti-fluoride.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.880
Years before COVID,

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.000
the antifluoridation crusade
was considered a case study

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.440
of "digital pandemics of
public health misinformation."

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.960
In the year before COVID,

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.520
the first worldwide survey

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.840
of the crisis of confidence
in science

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.440
of 140,000 people
in 140 countries

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.880
found that only
18 percent of humanity

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.400
appeared to have a "high" level
of trust in science.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.920
To my pleasant surprise though,

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.680
despite so many
institutional failures,

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.680
a 2020 follow-up of the survey
found trust in science

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.640
actually increased after COVID.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:03.120
Where does the science land
on water fluoridation?

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.960
First, let me address efficacy.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.000
The CDC attributes the steep
decline in dental decay

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.120
in the United States in the
latter half of the 20th century

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.040
to water fluoridation,

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.560
but similar declines were noted
in non-fluoridated countries,

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.720
attributed in large part to the
widespread global distribution

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.160
of fluoride toothpaste.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.400
The best evidence we have

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.280
comes from prospective studies
with concurrent controls,

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.360
comparing cavity rates over time

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.320
in fluoridated versus
non-fluoridated populations.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:32.800
There have been more than 100
such studies to date,

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.240
and overall,

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:37.920
fluoridation results in
35 percent fewer decayed,

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.280
missing, or filled baby teeth

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.200
and 26 percent fewer
decayed, missing,

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.400
or filled permanent teeth.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.000
So, community fluoridation
does indeed help

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.120
to cut down on cavities.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:51.640
The question then becomes,
at what cost,

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.259
which we'll discuss next.

00:05:55.591 --> 00:05:56.960
Naturally
fluoridated waters

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.600
up around two parts per million

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.480
can put children
under the age of nine

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.560
at increased risk
for dental fluorosis,

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.800
and a lifetime of drinking water
at four ppm can cause

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.120
skeletal fluorosis and increase
the risk of bone fractures.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:13.160
You can see these kinds of
levels in the Earth's natural

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:16.200
fluoride belts that extend
from Turkey through Iraq, Iran,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.120
and Afghanistan
to China and Japan.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.160
The reason susceptibility
to dental fluorosis ends

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.760
at around eight years old

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.800
is that's when enamel
maturation is completed,

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:30.000
before our final permanent teeth
finish erupting.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.240
After teeth are formed,

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:34.600
dental fluorosis can no longer
develop or worsen.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.760
At one ppm, one part
per million of fluoride,

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:39.640
public health authorities
estimated that less than

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.720
10 percent of kids
would develop the condition,

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.760
and only in its mildest forms.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.040
We've since learned that
the prevalence and severity

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.760
of fluorosis is much higher
than predicted.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:49.800
According to the CDC,

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.280
about a third of American
children now have some form

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.120
of dental fluorosis,

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.040
with about one in 30
experiencing

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.120
a moderate to severe case.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.360
This may reflect exposure
to multiple fluoride sources

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:04.480
not factored into
the original calculations.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:09.040
Now, most fluorosis is so mild
as to be hardly noticeable,

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:11.640
taking the form
of white streaks or splotches

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:12.800
visible only to dentists

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.760
under the bright lights
of their exam chair.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:19.280
But serious cases can involve
severe pitting and discoloration

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:22.440
and present more than just
a cosmetic defect.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:25.200
For example, one study found
that children with severe cases

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:29.040
are more likely to be viewed by
their peers as less attractive,

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.840
less careful, less clean,
less happy, less healthy,

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:36.520
less intelligent, less kind,
less reliable, less social.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:40.960
Imagine what that could do
to a kid's self-esteem.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.720
Given the higher-than-expected
rates of fluorosis,

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.840
in 2015,
the U.S. Public Health Service

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.720
reduced the recommended fluoride
concentration of drinking water

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:52.360
down to 0.7 ppm
across the board.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:56.600
Previously, levels were set at
up to 1.2 ppm in cooler areas

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.840
where people tend
to drink less water.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:01.480
This change would be estimated
to keep the percentage

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:04.440
of those developing fluorosis
of "aesthetic concern"

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:06.320
down to approximately
12 percent.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:09.040
In terms of other health
concerns, until recently,

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:12.920
mainstream medicine's view might
have perhaps best been summed up

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:16.080
by the final statement in
an exhaustive report published

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.200
by Consumer Reports in 1978:

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.360
"The simple truth is that

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.480
there is no
scientific controversy

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.920
over the safety of fluoridation.

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.920
The practice is safe,
economical, and beneficial.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:29.440
The survival
of this fake controversy,

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.160
in the Consumer Union's opinion,

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:34.360
is one of the major triumphs
of quackery over science

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.480
in our generation."

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.680
In the last few years, though,

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:41.080
there have been growing concerns
about the adverse effects

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.400
of fluoride
on brain development,

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:48.274
which I'll address next.

00:08:48.611 --> 00:08:51.480
Fluoride&nbsp;had been found to be
a developmental neurotoxin

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.480
in rats and mice,

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:54.520
leading to learning
and memory deficits,

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:57.760
which led to an interest
in studying human populations.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:58.960
Starting in the 1980s,

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.240
reports started appearing
in Chinese medical journals

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.080
that found correlations
between areas

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:05.600
naturally containing higher
fluoride levels in water

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:08.640
with lower intelligence
among children.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:11.920
Dental fluorosis, the
fluoride-induced tooth mottling,

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.280
is widespread in China,

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.080
with more than
90 million residents affected,

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:18.440
often in small pockets
surrounding particular

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.560
small springs
or mountain sources.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.400
Researchers took
advantage of the fact

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.080
that even adjoining
neighborhoods could have

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.080
wildly different
fluoride exposure,

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.360
setting up a type
of natural experiment.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.840
Due to limited access
to Chinese journals at the time,

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.880
these studies largely
escaped the attention

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.440
of scientists in the West

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.080
until a meta-analysis
of 16 such studies

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.880
was published in English
in 2008.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:45.920
"Fluoride and Children's
Intelligence: A Meta-analysis"

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.920
found that children living
in areas prone to fluorosis

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:52.320
had five times higher odds
of developing low IQ

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.280
than those living in areas
with little or no fluorosis.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.120
So, here we were,

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:59.400
thinking dental fluorosis
was just a cosmetic blemish,

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.800
but it may instead
be a visual indicator

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:04.280
of intellectual deficits.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:06.440
A subsequent
meta-analysis in 2012

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.320
including about 10 more studies

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.600
found that the average
intelligence gap between

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:14.880
high and low fluoride exposure
areas was about seven IQ points.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.560
By far the largest study,
involving thousands of children,

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:21.640
it found that even
at fluoride levels below 1 ppm,

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.440
higher fluoride levels
were associated with

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.760
a large drop
in the chances of developing

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:27.360
excellent intelligence,

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.320
defined as an IQ
of 130 or higher.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.560
Even very mild fluorosis was
associated with less than half

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:37.040
the odds of reaching
such a high IQ.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:40.120
By now, there have been
more than 50 studies showing

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.840
an association between higher
fluoride exposure and lower IQ.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:46.160
In the latest systematic
review meta-analysis,

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.640
90 percent of the studies
published in the last ten years

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:50.040
reported a link between

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:53.280
high fluoride exposure
and reduced intelligence.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:56.600
However, serious caveats
are in order.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:59.240
First, the fluoride
concentrations

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:00.080
in most of these studies

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:02.240
were well above
fluoridation levels.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.400
In the 2012 meta-analysis,
for example, one study clocked

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.800
concentrations
as high as 11.5 ppm,

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:12.880
far exceeding the US target
of 0.7 parts per million

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.480
as well as
the average concentration

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.280
in the United States,

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:18.560
which is around 0.8 ppm
in municipal water

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.160
and 0.3 ppm in well water.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.880
Now, to be fair,

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:26.280
the 11.5 ppm in the
meta-analysis was an outlier.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.560
The average elevated level
was only about

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:29.800
two parts per million,

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.200
and most found
associated IQ decrements

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:34.240
below the EPA's upper limit,

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:37.800
its Maximum Contaminant Level
Goal of four ppm,

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.520
which is supposed
to represent the level

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:43.720
"below which there is no known
or expected risk to health."

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.560
Some studies showed
lower intelligence

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:48.880
with fluoride concentrations
even down at one to two ppm

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.160
with one estimate suggesting

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.640
the smallest harmful
concentration,

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:55.080
potentially shaving off
a single IQ point,

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:58.080
would be down around 0.3 ppm,

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.320
assuming you drink
four cups of water a day,

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.520
while others suggest
it's too early to be able

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:05.320
to calculate a threshold
for human neurotoxicity

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.880
due to insufficient
available data.

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:11.600
The second major caveat
is confounding.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:14.120
Nearly all of the studies
to date have been performed

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.320
in rural communities
in countries like China,

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.080
Iran, and Mongolia.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.360
Areas within these countries

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.400
with unusually high
fluoride levels

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.760
may be particularly
poor and underdeveloped,

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.440
since relatively
rich communities

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:28.360
may be more likely to invest
in higher-quality drinking water

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:29.600
that filters out fluoride,

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:32.480
if only to reduce
dental fluorosis.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.560
High fluoride water may also be
more likely to be contaminated

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.920
with other neurotoxins.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:41.560
Fluoride exists in water as
a negatively charged particle.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.920
To maintain electroneutrality,

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.920
this may pull
into the groundwater

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:48.000
positively charged particles
such as aluminum,

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.360
arsenic, lead, or mercury.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:52.560
This doesn't happen
in community water fluoridation

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:55.240
since the negative fluoride ions
are balanced out

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:58.000
in the water treatment process.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.640
Finally,
most of the older studies

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:01.840
were cross-sectional
and ecological,

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.280
meaning they looked
at a snapshot-in-time

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:09.120
of group level data rather than
individual-exposures-over-time.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:13.400
Just because a child with low IQ
lives in a high fluoride area

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:15.680
doesn't necessarily mean
they or their mom actually

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.720
drank the water, for example.

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:21.200
Ideally, we'd be able to measure
individual exposure levels

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:23.280
and then follow
the kids over time

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:25.000
to see if those
with higher exposure

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.623
really do grow up
with stunted intellects.

